{
  "description": "Installation of one freestanding automated flower vending machine on the public footway directly in front of the existing ground-floor shop (Gaska), 301 High Road Leyton, positioned against the shopfront to the right of the shop entrance.\n\nThe machine measures approximately 2.0 m wide x 0.6 m deep x 2.18 m high, rising to 2.52 m including the roof canopy. It will be securely bolted to the ground and positioned tight against the shopfront, leaving approximately 3.5 m of clear, unobstructed footway for pedestrians, wheelchair users and pushchairs.\n\nThe machine sells fresh flower bouquets 24 hours a day by contactless card payment only and is powered from the shop’s existing electrical supply. It carries an internally illuminated “À la mienne” branded sign panel.\n\nNo structural alterations to the existing building and no change of use of the shop are proposed. The applicant will seek the necessary licence from the Council as highway authority for the placement of the machine on the footway.",
